# Cauliflower Lime Burrito Bowl

Based on [[https://www.mealime.com/recipes/…](https://www.mealime.com/recipes/roasted-cauliflower-black-bean-burrito-bow>425F) (wayback unavailable) (wayback unavailable) with an olive oil and spice l-cilantro-lime-rice/7720](https://www.mealime.com/recipes/roasted-cauliflower-black-bean-burrito-bowl-cilantro-lime-rice/7720).
Cauliflower in Instant Pot inspired by [https://www.pressurecookrecipes.com/instant-pot-cauliflower/…](https://www.pressurecookrecipes.com/instant-pot-cauliflower/) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250805101505/https://www.pressurecookrecipes.com/instant-pot-cauliflower/))

{ rating="5" image="cauliflower_lime_burrito_bowl.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Bowl

- [ ] 1 head [cauliflower]{ ing="cauliflower" }
- [ ] 1 cup [basmati rice]{ ing="basmati-rice" }, quinoa, etc.
- [ ] 1 [yellow onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" }, diced
- [ ] 1 (15 oz) can [black beans]{ ing="black-beans" }, rinsed
- [ ] 1 (15 oz) can [corn]{ ing="corn" }, rinsed

### Chili Powder Spices

Previously included 1 Tbsp chili powder and 1/2 tsp of the rest, but I calculated an approximate substitute based on: [https://www.spendwithpennies.com/homemade-chili-powde/…](https://www.spendwithpennies.com/homemade-chili-powder) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251207224944/https://www.spendwithpennies.com/homemade-chili-powder/))

- [ ] 1 tsp [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [garlic powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [onion powder]{ ing="onion-powder" }
- [ ] 3/4 tsp [cumin]{ ing="cumin" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [dried oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }

### Toppings

Note: this serves 4, so save one of each for the 2nd day

- [ ] 2 [avocados]{ ing="avocados" }, diced
- [ ] 2 [limes]{ ing="limes" }, diced
- [ ] 2 [tomatoes]{ ing="tomatoes" }, diced
- [ ] 1 small bunch [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, remove and mince the leaves
- [ ] (Optional) [salsa]{ ing="salsa" }

## Recipe

1. Pour 1 cup of water and place the trivet in the Instant Pot

   1. Remove _most of_ the leaves from the [Cauliflower]{ ing="cauliflower" }
   1. Cook for “0” min at high pressure (if longer, will be too soft)
   1. Once at pressure, quick release
   1. Remove the [cauliflower]{ ing="cauliflower" } to cool
1. Prep the spice mix
1. In a large skillet, on medium heat, saute the [onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" } with half of the spices
1. Rinse the [rice]{ ing="basmati-rice" } and store in 2-cup measure (and save strainer for [beans]{ ing="black-beans" } and [corn]{ ing="corn" })

   1. In the Instant Pot, combine [rice]{ ing="basmati-rice" } and water at a 1:1.5 ratio with broth or water
   1. Cook for 8 min at high pressure
   1. Quick release
   1. Add juice of 1 [lime]{ ing="limes" } per cup of [rice]{ ing="basmati-rice" } and fluff
1. Add the [beans]{ ing="black-beans" } and [corn]{ ing="corn" } to the pan
1. Once cool enough, remove the remaining leaves, chop the [cauliflower]{ ing="cauliflower" } into bite size pieces, and add to the pan

   1. Coat with remaining spices
1. Serve in bowls with diced toppings

## Notes

1. The cauliflower can also be roasted at >425F. Chop into bite size pieces, coat with olive oil and half of spices, then roast for 20 minutes
